## Issue context
Title: feat(release-readiness): workspace-hub-only model-release readiness contract and upgrade playbook
URL: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2408

Issue body:
## Summary
Split the broad #2399 model-release-readiness effort into a narrower, approval-friendly issue focused only on the workspace-hub control plane. Define the standing readiness contract and upgrade playbook for workspace-hub itself, without claiming full tier-1 ecosystem coverage.

## Why
Adversarial review on #2399 converged that the monolithic repo-ecosystem scope is too broad for a single T2 planning issue. A narrower workspace-hub-only contract is the cleanest first slice and provides the canonical base that later tier-1 work can consume.

## Scope
- define workspace-hub model-release readiness dimensions
- define discoverability anchors from existing control-plane entrypoints
- define upgrade playbook for new provider/model releases in workspace-hub
- define contract boundaries relative to `CONTROL_PLANE_CONTRACT.md`
- do not claim tier-1 repo inventory completeness in this issue

## Deliverables
1. `docs/standards/MODEL_RELEASE_READINESS_CONTRACT.md`
2. `docs/standards/MODEL_RELEASE_UPGRADE_PLAYBOOK.md`
3. discoverability-anchor updates in canonical workspace-hub entrypoints
4. a concise workspace-hub-only gap summary

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] contract explicitly covers context-budget/truncation-safe artifact design
- [ ] contract explicitly covers machine-readable rules/skills vs prose-only guidance
- [ ] contract explicitly covers prompt-pack portability for workspace-hub workflows
- [ ] discoverability anchors exist in the chosen canonical entrypoints
- [ ] issue stays scoped to workspace-hub, not the full repo ecosystem

## Parent
- #2399


